em", "numeric-id": 918, "id": "Q918"}, "type": "wikibase-entityid"}, "datatype": "wikibase-item"}, "type": "statement", "id": "Q9382$1127A194-A7B6-40A1-9C9E-503989EA107D", "rank": "normal"}], "P19": [{"mainsnak": {"snaktype": "value", "property": "P19", "hash": "436a6877dca39aabfb6f2503506f935997ae1b75", "datavalue": {"value": "Yeah. But it was me and Richard Williams, that was the trumpet section, and Slide Hampton and Garnett Brown was in the trombone section. Let's see. Hubert Laws was playing tenor saxophone. And I can't remember who else was in the band. But I mean it was a great band. And Slide was very popular. He'd had a hit, kind of a hit at that time, called \"Sister Salvation,\" so we played all of this music...", "type": "string"}, "datatype": "string"}, "type": "statement", "id": "Q9382$1F883B5C-8E07-4FBA-A0C0-6D538841DD88", "rank": "normal"}]}}